---
description: Rules for provider integrations and external APIs
globs: ["server/**/*.ts", "src/lib/**/*.ts", "src/pages/**/*.{ts,tsx}", "src/components/**/*.{ts,tsx}"]
---

Integration rules:
- isolate provider-specific logic as much as possible
- do not spread API-specific behavior across pages and components
- prefer dedicated helpers, services, or adapter modules for external providers
- normalize external responses into internal shapes when reasonable
- handle rate limits, retries, and partial failures explicitly
- never hardcode secrets, tokens, or account identifiers
- preserve current app behavior while improving integration boundaries incrementally

When working on integrations:
- first identify what is provider-specific and what is app-specific
- avoid introducing large abstraction layers unless clearly needed